Fixed. The error happened because `Dashboard` calls `useRootContext()`, but nothing in the tree was rendering `RootProvider`. I wrapped the whole app shell in it — [App.tsx](marketlab/src/App.tsx) now imports `RootProvider` from `./context/RootContext` and wraps the entire layout, so every page has access to user/theme/currency context. TypeScript passes clean (`tsc --noEmit` exit 0) and Vite transforms the file without errors, so the running dev server has already hot-reloaded the fix — reload the page and the crash is gone.

## Commands to run the application

**Frontend** (this is what's running now):

```bash
cd marketlab
npm install        # first time only
npm run dev        # starts Vite at http://localhost:5176
```

Production build check:

```bash
cd marketlab
npm run build      # outputs to marketlab/dist
```

**Backend** (Convex functions in [marketlab/convex](marketlab/convex)):

```bash
cd marketlab
npm install convex @convex-dev/convex   # not yet in package.json — one-time
npx convex dev                          # deploys functions + starts local backend
```

Important caveat: there is **no backend process today**. `convex` isn't installed as a dependency yet, and the frontend talks to a typed mock layer ([src/convex/_generated/api.ts](marketlab/src/convex/_generated/api.ts)) rather than a live Convex deployment — that's why the app runs with just `npm run dev` and no second terminal. `npx convex dev` will prompt you to log in and create/select a Convex project, give you a `CONVEX_URL` for `.env.local`, and run your schema and functions for real. Until that's wired up, data doesn't persist between sessions.

If you only want the app on screen right now: `cd marketlab && npm run dev`, then open http://localhost:5176 (already registered in the Preview tab).
