{"kind":"agent","id":"bm0ygnPBCXM","agentType":"researcher-web","displayName":"Web Researcher","prompt":"Question about the Convex CLI (convex.dev): when running `npx convex dev` for the first time in a new project, what exactly happens — does it require interactive login/signup (browser OAuth, email), and are there non-interactive alternatives (CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY, CONVEX_EMAIL/CONVEX_PASSWORD env vars, `npx convex login` beforehand, CI provisioning, `convex dev --local` / local-only development without an account)? Also: is there any way to run a fully local Convex backend (self-hosted or local mode) for development without a Convex cloud account? Report exact commands and flags from official docs (convex.dev/docs, docs.convex.dev, GitHub convexdev/convex-cli or convex repo), with URLs. Also note what `npx convex codegen` does and whether it requires login.","status":"done","blocks":[{"kind":"tool","id":"bm1BpT0b0As","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:docs.convex.dev npx convex dev first time login deploy key local mode codegen login","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"bm2J-h-12NM","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:github.com/get-convex/convex-cli CONVEX_EMAIL CONVEX_PASSWORD CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY convex login","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"bm3S5mUC1CI","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:docs.convex.dev self-hosted local backend convex dev --local account","depth":"standard"}},{"kind":"tool","id":"bm4NJow3fVI","toolName":"web_search","input":{"query":"site:docs.convex.dev codegen requires login convex codegen" [… 6,989 characters omitted] ate a new cloud project. Creating keys with `npx convex deployment token create` itself requires an already logged-in personal account; teams commonly provision keys in advance through the dashboard or setup tooling. ([Deploy Keys](https://docs.convex.dev/cli/deploy-key-types), [Agent Mode](https://docs.convex.dev/cli/agent-mode))
- **`CONVEX_EMAIL` / `CONVEX_PASSWORD`:** I found no support for these as CLI login variables in the official documentation reviewed. The documented non-interactive credential is **`CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY`**; don’t rely on email/password environment variables unless a separate, version-specific official source documents them.
- **`npx convex login` beforehand:** This is supported and useful to avoid doing the account-login step during project setup. It still requires the user to authenticate once, and it does **not** remove the need to choose/configure a project or deployment if one isn’t configured.

### Fully local backend and self-hosting

**Yes, you can develop against a fully local Convex backend without a cloud account** using Convex’s local deployments/anonymous development. It’s a local development deployment, not a cloud deployment; the docs note limitations such as no public URL for incoming webhooks and local-specific behavior. ([Local Deployments](https://docs.convex.dev/cli/local-deployments))

Separately, Convex also supports **self-hosting the open-source backend** on your own servers. That is distinct from simply selecting a local deployment and involves running/operating the backend yourself; the self-hosting overview points to its separate guide. ([Self Hosting](https://docs.convex.dev/self-hosting))

### What `npx convex codegen` does—and login

```sh
npx convex codegen
```

This generates code in `convex/_generated/` from the project’s `convex/` contents. `npx convex dev` runs code generation automatically; explicit codegen is mainly useful for cases such as CI. The docs say it **can require communicating with a Convex deployment** to evaluate configuration files, but it does not change code running on the deployment. Thus, **codegen is not documented as inherently requiring a login**; whether it needs deployment access depends on the project/configuration. ([`codegen` reference](https://docs.convex.dev/cli/reference/codegen), [CLI overview](https://docs.convex.dev/cli/overview))"}]}
