## Phase 2 delivered — with one environment blocker I could not work around

Phase 2 is implemented end to end and the code checks pass, but **this machine will not let the Convex backend run**, so I could not push the schema, regenerate the official API types, or exercise authenticated data flows in the browser.

### The blocker (read this first)

```
✖ Failed to run backend binary: TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'toString')
```
The Convex CLI needs `convex-local-backend.exe`; the download succeeded (`https://github.com/convex/convex-backend/releases/download/precompiled-2026-10-10-72ce13c/...`, 49.7 MB, also placed in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\convex inaries\precompiled-2026-10-10-72ce13c\`), but Windows refuses to execute it:

> Program 'convex-local-backend.exe' failed to run: **An Application Control policy has blocked this file**

`Unblock-File` did not help; Docker is not installed. Consequence: `npx convex dev`, `npx convex codegen` and therefore `convex/_generated/api.d.ts` regeneration all fail here. **On a machine where that binary is allowed**, run `npx convex dev` once — it pushes the schema, validates every function and regenerates `_generated/`. Until then the new API is called through typed `makeFunctionReference` bindings in [marketClient.ts](marketlab/src/lib/marketClient.ts), so the app type-checks against real argument/return types without hand-editing generated files.

### What I built

**Backend (new)** — [convex/market/](marketlab/convex/market): `types.ts`, `time.ts` (IST, sessions, chunking), `normalize.ts` (validation, de-dup, gaps, freshness, redaction), `indicators.ts` (SMA/EMA/RSI/MACD/Bollinger/VWAP), `csv.ts`, `sample.ts`, `rateLimit.ts`, `hash.ts`, `registry.ts`, `providers/{fyers,breeze,tapetide}.ts`; plus [marketData.ts](marketlab/convex/marketData.ts), [marketStore.ts](marketlab/convex/marketStore.ts), [screener.ts](marketlab/convex/screener.ts), [chartPreferences.ts](marketlab/convex/chartPreferences.ts), and the extended [schema.ts](marketlab/convex/schema.ts) (`marketQuotes`, `fundamentals`, `candleDatasets`, `candles`, `providerState`, `marketCalendar`, `savedScreeners`, `chartPreferences`, `dataImports`, instrument search indexes).

**Frontend (new/changed)** — [PriceChart.tsx](marketlab/src/components/chart/PriceChart.tsx) (lightweight-charts 5.2.1, Apache-2.0), [DataModeBadge.tsx](marketlab/src/components/market/DataModeBadge.tsx), [useQuotes.ts](marketlab/src/hooks/useQuotes.ts) (one batched request per page), [marketClient.ts](marketlab/src/lib/marketClient.ts), [format.ts](marketlab/src/lib/format.ts), [Markets.tsx](marketlab/src/pages/Markets.tsx), [InstrumentDetail.tsx](marketlab/src/pages/InstrumentDetail.tsx), [Screener.tsx](marketlab/src/pages/Screener.tsx), [DataSources.tsx](marketlab/src/pages/DataSources.tsx), [Dashboard.tsx](marketlab/src/pages/Dashboard.tsx), [App.tsx](marketlab/src/App.tsx), [Watchlists.tsx](marketlab/src/pages/Watchlists.tsx) (resolves synced instrument ids), [select.tsx](marketlab/src/components/ui/select.tsx) (shows labels, follows `value`).

**One notable change:** the existing markup was written in Tailwind utilities but Tailwind was never installed, so those classes did nothing. I added Tailwind 3 + PostCSS ([tailwind.config.js](marketlab/tailwind.config.js), [postcss.config.js](marketlab/postcss.config.js)) so the *existing* design renders as authored — no markup or layout redesign.

### Providers — declared capabilities only

| | FYERS | Breeze | Tapetide |
|---|---|---|---|
| Instruments / sync | ✅ public `sym_details` CSV, layout auto-detected | ⚠️ master is a ZIP → CSV import only | ✅ search route |
| Quotes | ✅ 50/call | ✅ 1/call | ✅ 20/call, `DELAYED` |
| Candles | 1m 5m 15m 1h 1D 1W 1M | 1m 5m 1d only (15m/1h refused, never resampled) | ❌ not claimed (params unverifiable) |
| Fundamentals | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ quote + statements |
| Streaming | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |

Streaming is deliberately **off**: both brokers expose websockets, but a persistent socket host is outside a Convex serverless deployment. Quotes are server-mediated with caching + per-minute/daily quota limits and honest freshness labels. Endpoints follow the current official docs (FYERS `/data/quotes`, `/data/history`, `/api/v3/validate-authcode`, `/validate-refresh-token`; Breeze `quotes`, `historicalcharts` with `X-Checksum = token sha256(timestamp+body+secret)`; Tapetide `/v1/quotes`, `/stocks/{s}/quote`, `/financials`, `/me/usage`).

### Environment variables (backend only, never `VITE_`)

`FYERS_APP_ID`, `FYERS_SECRET_ID`, `FYERS_ACCESS_TOKEN`, optional `FYERS_REFRESH_TOKEN` · `BREEZE_APP_KEY`, `BREEZE_SECRET_KEY`, `BREEZE_SESSION_TOKEN` · `TAPETIDE_API_TOKEN`

You must obtain these yourself: a FYERS app with the **Market Data** permission (tokens expire daily 06:30 IST); an ICICI Breeze app plus an **interactive customer login** session token (~24 h) — an AppKey alone cannot read data; optionally a Tapetide personal token. Set them with `npx convex env set NAME value` (a local `.env.local` does **not** reach Convex functions). The Data Sources page prints these exact commands and lists missing names only — values are never read back.

### Limits and licensing (unresolved, dev-use only)

FYERS: ~1 yr intraday / ~5 yr daily on Standard, 100/366-day per request. Breeze: 100 calls/min, 5,000/day, 1000 candles/request. Tapetide: 50 successful calls per IST day, 60/min burst. Redistribution is **not** granted by any of them — Breeze terms forbid sublicensing and sharing credentials, FYERS/exchange permission is needed, Tapetide prohibits redistribution. Keep the app in development until you have written authorisation.

### Verified (commands actually run)

- `npx tsc --noEmit` → **exit 0**
- `npx vitest run` → **62/62 passing** across 4 files (indicators + warm-up, SHA-256 vectors, rate/quota windows, IST & FYERS epoch conversion, session/holiday status, CSV validation & rejection lines & duplicates, normalization/de-dup/gaps, **stale data never labelled LIVE**, redaction, missing-credential reporting, Breeze interval refusal, FYERS CSV column detection, sample determinism & session bounds)
- `npx vite build` → **success** (510 kB JS / 21 kB CSS; chunk-size warning only)
- Browser: chart renders 130 sample candles with volume + SMA/Bollinger overlays and an RSI pane, correct badges, no console errors; Markets, Data Sources and the new sidebar routes mount cleanly; only expected `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` to `127.0.0.1:3210`.
- Backend type check of `convex/**` shows **only** errors caused by the stale generated API (missing `marketStore`/`marketData` entries); the real errors it surfaced were fixed (CSV header map, `csv_import` candle source, screener row typing).

**Not verified** (backend unavailable): Convex push/schema validation, sign-in + ownership enforcement for the new tables, persisted screener/chart preferences, provider connection tests, live instrument sync, CSV import against a real deployment, and a full explorer-with-data browser test. The Vite dev server is running at http://localhost:5173 (PID 78472) — sign-in, watchlists and quotes stay in loading/error states until `npx convex dev` works.

Nothing is committed yet; the working tree holds 11 modified files and 30 new ones, with `.env.local` and logs still ignored.

Two things worth doing next: getting the backend running so the new schema and ownership checks can actually be exercised, and then wiring the quotes you already label correctly into the paper-trading flow that Phase 3 depends on.
