Phase 6 is implemented and verified. No live-money trading, no production deployment, and no new provider was added.

## 1. Features implemented and files changed

**Provider integration hardening — IMPLEMENTED, TESTED (mock-only)**
- New [`convex/market/http.ts`](marketlab/convex/market/http.ts): `fetchWithTimeout` (15 s default) and `ProviderTimeoutError`. All outbound calls in the FYERS, Breeze and Tapetide adapters now go through it, so a hung socket fails as “Provider request timed out after N ms” instead of burning the action budget.
- Fixed a real redaction defect in [`convex/market/normalize.ts`](marketlab/convex/market/normalize.ts): the secret regex ate the word after “token”, turning actionable messages into `token=<redacted>`. It now redacts only `key=value` bindings or values ≥ 8 characters, so “access token has expired” survives while `token=eyJ…` is still removed.
- Re-phrased the FYERS expired-session message in [`fyers.ts`](marketlab/convex/market/providers/fyers.ts) so it stays readable after redaction.
- New [`tests/providerAdapters.test.ts`](marketlab/tests/providerAdapters.test.ts): 15 tests covering timeout conversion, missing-credential behaviour for all three providers, FYERS quote normalisation and DELAYED labelling, expired-session messaging, token non-leakage, candle row validation/sorting, Breeze IST→UTC conversion, Breeze refusing `15m` instead of resampling, registry precedence, and explicit capability reporting.

**Alerts completion — IMPLEMENTED, TESTED, browser-verified**
- New `alerts.update` mutation in [`convex/alerts.ts`](marketlab/convex/alerts.ts): validates the threshold server-side, re-checks owner, and refuses to edit a TRIGGERED alert (it must be re-armed first, since its trigger record is history).
- [`Alerts.tsx`](marketlab/src/pages/Alerts.tsx) gained an Edit flow: pre-fills direction/threshold/note, locks the instrument, offers Update/Cancel, and returns to “New alert” on completion.

**Performance and deployment readiness — IMPLEMENTED, TESTED**
- [`vite.config.ts`](marketlab/vite.config.ts) now splits `react`, `convex`, `charts` and `vendor` chunks. The >500 kB warning is gone; largest chunk is 180 kB (49 kB gzip).
- New [`docs/provider-and-simulation-notes.md`](marketlab/docs/provider-and-simulation-notes.md): provider matrix, labelling rules, why alerts are manual, the backtest-vs-paper fill comparison table, and remaining limitations.

**No changes were needed** to the paper engine, ledger, ownership checks or backtest core — the audit found them sound; see verification below.

## 2. Tests

```
npx vitest run → 19 files, 277 tests passed (262 before this phase), 0 failed
```
The 15 new tests are the provider-adapter contract suite. All deterministic; no network access.

## 3. TypeScript and build

```
npx tsc --noEmit  → clean, no output
npx vite build    → success
  index.html 0.83 kB · index.css 34.49 kB
  vendor 38.06 kB · convex 86.51 kB · react 142.93 kB · charts 166.74 kB · index 180.04 kB
```

## 4. Browser workflows actually tested

- **1440×900**: dashboard renders 4 columns, `scrollWidth === innerWidth` (no overflow); Alerts page no overflow.
- **390×844**: Alerts page no page-level overflow, wide table scrolls inside its container, mobile menu toggle visible.
- **Alert lifecycle**: re-armed a triggered alert → Edit appeared → changed threshold 100 → 2,100 → “Alert updated” → condition shown as `Price ≥ ₹2,100.00` → survived a reload as `ACTIVE` with `Edit/Pause/Delete`.
- **Idempotent orders** (test account B): submitted the same `clientOrderId` twice; second response returned `duplicate: true` with the same fill price, only **one** order existed, and cash was debited once (₹1,00,000 → ₹97,353.53 for 1 × INFY at ₹2,646.47, labelled SAMPLE).
- **Signed-out access**: `watchlists:create` without a token was rejected.

## 5. Two-user isolation — PERFORMED, PASSED

Two real authenticated sessions (Password provider): User A had 1 alert, 1 watchlist with an item, 1 strategy, 1 backtest run, 1 filled order. User B was created in an isolated incognito profile and used its own JWT to attack A’s record IDs directly over the Convex HTTP API:

| Attempt | Result |
|---|---|
| `backtests:get` with A’s run id | returned `null` |
| `alerts:remove` A’s alert | rejected — “Not authorized” |
| `alerts:update` A’s alert | rejected — “Not authorized” |
| `watchlists:rename` A’s list | rejected — “Not authorized” |
| `watchlists:removeItem` A’s item | rejected — “Not authorized” |
| `strategies:remove` A’s strategy | rejected — “Strategy not found” |
| `backtests:remove` A’s run | rejected — “Run not found” |
| `paper:cancelOrder` A’s order | rejected — “Order not found” |

B could create and read **its own** watchlist and alert (`B private list` visible only to B; A’s lists stayed `["Phase 5 Core"]`). After all attempts, A’s records were unchanged: alert threshold 2,100 / ACTIVE, 1 list, 1 strategy, 1 run, 1 FILLED order. Tokens were read only inside the page and never printed.

## 6. Provider status: UNVERIFIED (mock-only)

| Provider | Implemented | Live credential test |
|---|---|---|
| FYERS (quotes, history, symbol master; 1m–1M) | Quotes + candles + ready | **UNVERIFIED** — no credentials |
| Breeze (quotes, `historicalcharts`; 1m/5m/1d) | Quotes + candles ready | **UNVERIFIED** — no credentials; session token needs interactive ICICI login |
| Tapetide (quotes only) | Quotes + fundamentals ready | **UNVERIFIED** — no credentials |

No successful live response was fabricated. The cache, rate-limit and fallback paths were reviewed in code; the “failed provider → labelled SAMPLE with an explicit warning” path exists in `marketData.getCandles` but is **not covered by an automated test** (it needs a Convex test harness), so treat it as reviewed, not proven.

## 7. Remaining limitations

- **No market-data credentials** — every quote, fill and alert trigger in this deployment is SAMPLE; nothing is labelled LIVE.
- **Alerts are manual only.** No cron, no email/push. A scheduled job would currently only ever read SAMPLE quotes, which would imply real-price monitoring that does not exist; the UI and docs say so.
- **No streaming** (`streaming` unsupported for all providers), **no exchange holiday calendar**, **no brokerage/tax/slippage** in paper fills, and backtests stay bounded (5,000 candles / 500 stored trades).
- **Legitimate simulation differences** are documented in the new notes file rather than unified: backtests fill at the next candle open with configurable costs; paper fills at the quote immediately with no costs.
- A test account `phase6.userb@example.test` exists in the dev deployment with one sample order; A’s demo records (alert, watchlist, strategy, run, order) were left in place.

## 8. Scope confirmation

No broker order placement, no real-money execution, no options/margin/shorting, no production deployment and no paid service was introduced. All work is against the local development Convex deployment and local Vite server.

Status summary: **IMPLEMENTED & TESTED** — provider timeouts/redaction contract, alert editing, chunk splitting, docs, isolation; **LIVE-VERIFIED** — alert edit persistence, order idempotency, two-user ownership, desktop/mobile layout; **UNVERIFIED** — every real provider request (no credentials) and the provider-failure→SAMPLE fallback path.
